---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Umrah Visa for Pakistanis — Complete 2026 Guide',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'VisaPath.pk' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'VisaPath.pk' },
  datePublished: '2026-10-24',
};

const faq = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How long is Umrah visa valid?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Umrah visa is valid for 90 days from issue date, allowing travel to Saudi Arabia for Umrah pilgrimage. Stay inside Saudi Arabia is up to 90 days.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Can women perform Umrah without mahram?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Yes. Since 2021, women aged 18+ can perform Umrah without a mahram (male guardian) by applying through licensed agents or online Nusuk platform.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'What is Nusuk platform?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Nusuk is Saudi Arabia official platform for Umrah and Hajj pilgrims. It allows direct bookings for visa, Haram prayer times, hotels, and transport.' } },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Umrah Visa for Pakistanis — Complete 2026 Guide"
  description="How Pakistanis apply for Umrah visa, costs, requirements, Nusuk platform, female pilgrims, agent vs direct booking."
  schema={[article, faq]}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Home</a> ›
      <a href="/guides/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Guides</a> ›
      <span>Umrah Visa</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Umrah Visa for Pakistanis — Complete 2026 Guide</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mb-8">Last updated: October 2026 · 9 minute read</p>

    <section class="prose max-w-none">
      <p class="lead text-lg">
        Umrah is one of the most spiritually significant journeys for Pakistani Muslims. Saudi Arabia has significantly simplified the Umrah visa process since 2021 — this guide covers everything you need to know.
      </p>

      <h2>Umrah Visa Overview (2026)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Validity:</strong> 90 days from issue</li>
        <li><strong>Maximum stay:</strong> 90 days inside Saudi Arabia</li>
        <li><strong>Entries:</strong> single entry</li>
        <li><strong>Visa fee:</strong> approximately $300 USD (government + agent fees)</li>
        <li><strong>Entry points:</strong> Jeddah (JED) and Madinah (MED) airports</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Major Changes Since 2021</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Women can travel without mahram</strong> — women 18+ can perform Umrah independently</li>
        <li><strong>Travel anywhere in Saudi Arabia</strong> — not restricted to Makkah/Madinah</li>
        <li><strong>Online Nusuk platform</strong> — direct visa applications</li>
        <li><strong>Extended stay</strong> — from 30 days to 90 days</li>
        <li><strong>No age limit for pilgrims</strong> — removed previous restrictions</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Three Ways to Apply</h2>

      <h3>Option 1 — Through Pakistani Umrah Agent</h3>
      <p>
        The most common method. Ministry of Religious Affairs Pakistan (MORA) licenses Umrah agents who handle:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Visa application and processing</li>
        <li>Flight bookings</li>
        <li>Hotel reservations in Makkah and Madinah</li>
        <li>Transport within Saudi Arabia</li>
        <li>Group ziyarat tours</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Package costs:</strong> PKR 180,000 (budget economy) to PKR 500,000+ (VIP) per person for 10-day packages.
      </p>

      <h3>Option 2 — Nusuk Platform (Direct Online)</h3>
      <p>
        Saudi Arabia's official platform at <code>nusuk.sa</code> allows direct booking:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>Create Nusuk account</li>
        <li>Select "Umrah Visa" application</li>
        <li>Upload passport, photo, booking proofs</li>
        <li>Pay visa fee</li>
        <li>Book flights, hotels, and transport separately or through Nusuk partners</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Suitable for independent travelers familiar with online booking. Does not include any package services.
      </p>

      <h3>Option 3 — Transit Umrah (via Saudi carriers)</h3>
      <p>
        Saudia and flynas offer "Transit Umrah" — Pakistani passengers transiting through Jeddah or Riyadh can get a free short-stay Umrah visa (up to 96 hours).
      </p>

      <h2>Required Documents</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Pakistani passport valid 6+ months with 2 blank pages</li>
        <li>Recent photographs (passport size, white background)</li>
        <li>Vaccination certificates (as required — typically meningitis quadrivalent)</li>
        <li>Return flight ticket confirmation</li>
        <li>Hotel bookings in Makkah and Madinah</li>
        <li>Health insurance (recommended)</li>
        <li>Travel insurance (recommended)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Health Requirements</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Meningitis vaccination:</strong> ACYW135 strains, taken 10 days before and valid 3 years</li>
        <li><strong>COVID-19:</strong> requirements vary; check latest Saudi guidelines</li>
        <li><strong>Yellow fever:</strong> for pilgrims from certain African countries, not applicable to Pakistan</li>
        <li><strong>Seasonal flu vaccine:</strong> recommended, especially for seniors</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Visa Process Timeline</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Choose agent or self-apply</li>
        <li>Submit documents (passport, photo, bookings)</li>
        <li>Visa processing: typically 3–10 working days</li>
        <li>Visa stamped in passport or issued electronically</li>
        <li>Pay package / Nusuk fees</li>
        <li>Travel to Saudi Arabia</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Female Pilgrim Guidelines</h2>
      <p>
        Women traveling without mahram:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Must be 18 or older</li>
        <li>Preferred (not required) to travel in groups</li>
        <li>Can book through agents or Nusuk directly</li>
        <li>Must still observe hijab and modest dress</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children and Minors</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No minimum age for Umrah</li>
        <li>Must have own passport (even infants)</li>
        <li>Travel with parent(s) with birth certificate</li>
        <li>If one parent is absent, consent letter required</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Peak Seasons to Avoid (or Choose)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Ramadan (especially last 10 days):</strong> most spiritually significant but extremely crowded; prices triple</li>
        <li><strong>Hajj season (Dhul-Hijjah):</strong> Umrah visas restricted or suspended during Hajj period</li>
        <li><strong>School holidays (Jun–Aug):</strong> popular with Pakistani families, higher prices</li>
        <li><strong>Winter (Dec–Feb):</strong> cooler weather, moderate crowds, popular</li>
        <li><strong>Shoulder months (Mar, Nov):</strong> pleasant weather, good value</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What to Expect in Saudi Arabia</h2>
      <h3>Arrival</h3>
      <p>
        At Jeddah or Madinah airport, immigration checks your Umrah visa and biometric data. Expect queues during peak season.
      </p>

      <h3>Hotels</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Makkah:</strong> hotels near Haram (within 300m) are premium; shuttle service from further hotels</li>
        <li><strong>Madinah:</strong> hotels facing Masjid Nabawi are prime; most within 500m acceptable</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Transport Between Cities</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Haramain High-Speed Rail: 2.5 hours Makkah to Madinah</li>
        <li>Private coach/car: 4 hours</li>
        <li>Taxi/Uber available</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Rules to Follow</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Perform Umrah before leaving the country (or on return trip from Madinah)</li>
        <li>Do not overstay 90 days — fines up to SAR 100,000 and bans</li>
        <li>Do not work on Umrah visa — strict penalties</li>
        <li>Observe Saudi laws regarding dress, behavior, prayer times</li>
        <li>Keep passport and visa accessible at all times</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Common Mistakes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Choosing unlicensed agents — risk of scam</li>
        <li>Not vaccinating in time — denied boarding</li>
        <li>Booking during Hajj period — Umrah visas suspended</li>
        <li>Underestimating costs for Zamzam, souvenirs, extras</li>
        <li>Not keeping Ihram and prayer clothes in carry-on (checked bags can be lost)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Related Resources</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/tools/umrah-cost-calculator/">Umrah Cost Calculator</a> ·
        <a href="/tools/passport-validity-checker/">Passport Validity Checker (Saudi 6-month rule)</a> ·
        <a href="/guides/uae-visa-types-pakistan/">UAE Visa Guide (transit)</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
